          move forward and it speeds up, drift back and it slows. The AssaultRunner Pro is the
          best-known home version of that idea, and its core figures are consistent across
          Assault's listing and independent coverage. Its warranty is not, and its stock has been
          patchy. This page covers both, along with the more important question of whether a
          curved trainer suits the way you actually train.
        </p>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          14 October 2026 we read Assault Fitness's US product page for the AssaultRunner Pro,
          including its specification table, comparison table and FAQ, and cross-checked it against
          a US dealer listing (Push Pedal Pull) and two independent reviews published in 2024.
